Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `owner` was consumed by `close`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/close_temp_file_then_read_path.jet:7:17
    |
  7 |     print(owner.path)
    |                 ^^^^
  --> tests/ui/close_temp_file_then_read_path.jet:6:11
    |
  6 |     close(owner)
    |           ^^^^^ `owner` moved to `close` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `owner` after the move, or give `close` a copy with `owner.copy()` where it moved.
 Note: acquire a new `TempFile` resource; closed resources cannot be copied or reused
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
